\inchannels sets the number of audio input channels of
Python (pyo). The default is 2.
It takes one argument, an integer:

\inchannels 1

Like all audio settings, it must be called before \python
is called for the first time, otherwise it has no effect.

Note that currently the audio stream of LiveLily is opened
with output channels only, so this value is passed to pyo
but audio input is not streamed to it.

To set both input and output channels at once, use
\nchannels:

\nchannels 2
